content.text:
Now main.js. Add DOM refs. After `pauseScreen` refs and results refs. Let's insert:
```
const unlockNote = ...
const garageScreen...
...
```
After `resultKicker`. Also titleCarName, titleCarDot, garageBtn.

Then add catalog & garage functions after playerCar creation perhaps. Need `PLAYER_CARS`, `garageSave`, `isUnlocked`, `selectedCarSpec`, `loadGarage`, `saveGarage`, `meetsUnlock`, `applyPlayerSetup`, `renderGarage`, `openGarage`, `closeGarage`, `recordRaceResult`.

But some functions reference `startRace` (hoisted function declaration, fine), and DOM refs.

Where to put? After `const playerCar = cars.find...` but before `state`. `applyPlayerSetup` uses `titleCarName` refs (defined above). Fine. `renderGarage` uses `garageGrid` ref. Fine.

However, catalog must be defined before use. Player car def color etc. overridden later.

Let me write the code.

CAR_ICON function/markup: define a constant string with placeholders? Use a function `carIcon(spec)` returning string:
```
function carIcon(spec) {
 return `<svg viewBox="0 0 64 96" aria-hidden="true">
  <ellipse .../>
  <path ... fill="${spec.color}"/>
  ...
 </svg>`;
}
```
Stats: `statRow('SPD', spec.speed)`:
```
const pct = value => Math.round(clamp((value - 0.85) / 0.25, 0, 1) * 100);
```
Values:
- APEX speed 1 → 60%; too low. Better map: rating = Math.round(clamp((value - 0.85)/0.2,0,1)*70 + 30). But stats display bars; relative differences matter:
```
const rating = v => Math.round(clamp((v - 0.85) / 0.28, 0.25, 1) * 100);
```
APEX: (0.15/0.28)=0.536→54%. ONYX 1.03 → 64%. Not visually distinct. Use a fixed multiplier scale:
- speed 0.97..1.05: map to 55..95:
`Math.round(clamp(30 + (v - 0.9) * 250, 20, 100))` → v=1 → 55; 1.05→67. Still not distinct.

Since only 5 cars and bars are aesthetic, use explicit rating numbers in catalog: `ratings: { spd: 6, acc: 6, grip: 6 }` out of 10, with ONYX 8/8/8. Add to specs. Simpler and clearer. Let's include `stats: [6,6,6]` for APEX, JADE [6,7,9], BLAZE [7,9,5], NOVA [9,6,7], ONYX [9,9,9]. Display bars width `rating*10%`.

Catalog fields:
```
{ id:'apex', name:'APEX', tag:'BALANCED', color:'#3ae2ff', accent:'#0b7f96', number:1,
  speed:1, accel:1, grip:1, stats:[6,6,6], unlock:null }
{ id:'jade', name:'JADE', tag:'GRIP', color:'#86ef6a', accent:'#2f7a28', number:14,
  speed:0.98, accel:1.02, grip:1.08, stats:[6,7,9], unlock:{type:'races',count:1,label:'Finish 1 race'} }
{ id:'blaze', name:'BLAZE', tag:'LAUNCH', color:'#ff8a3d', accent:'#8f3a0d', number:23,
  speed:1.0, accel:1.12, grip:0.95, stats:[7,9,5], unlock:{type:'races',count:3,label:'Finish 3 races'} }
{ id:'nova', name:'NOVA', tag:'TOP END', color:'#ff5fd2', accent:'#7a1f62', number:5,
  speed:1.05, accel:0.98, grip:1.01, stats:[9,6,7], unlock:{type:'wins',count:1,label:'Win 1 race'} }
{ id:'onyx', name:'ONYX', tag:'PROTOTYPE', color:'#d5e0e2', accent:'#2a3437', number:0,
  speed:1.03, accel:1.03, grip:1.05, stats:[9,9,9], unlock:{type:'wins',count:3,label:'Win 3 races'} }
```
But NOVA magenta and AI GHOST violet may be similar. Fine. BLAZE orange and RIPPER red distinct enough.

Player speed 600 *1.05 = 630 px/s → 264.6 kmh. Gauge max 280. "not 300" still.

Apply:
```
playerCar.name = spec.name; ...
playerCar.maxSpeed = 600 * spec.speed;
playerCar.accel = 720 * spec.accel;
playerCar.grip = 7.6 * spec.grip;
```
But 600 and 720/7.6 are car.js defaults; add constants:
```
const BASE_PLAYER_SPEED = 600;
const BASE_PLAYER_ACCEL = 720;
const BASE_PLAYER_GRIP = 7.6;
```
Also AI stats unaffected.

localStorage key `apex-drift-garage-v1`.

Garage state:
```
const garageSave = { selected:'apex', races:0, wins:0, unlocked:['apex'] };
```
`loadGarage` validates.
`meetsUnlock` uses counts.
`unlockNewCars()` returns newly unlocked specs:
```
function unlockNewCars() {
 const found = [];
 for (const spec of PLAYER_CARS) {
   if (spec.unlock && !garageSave.unlocked.includes(spec.id) && meetsUnlock(spec)) { garageSave.unlocked.push(spec.id); found.push(spec); }
 }
 if (found.length) saveGarage();
 return found;
}
```
`recordRace(pos)`:
```
garageSave.races += 1;
if (pos===1) garageSave.wins += 1;
const unlocked = unlockNewCars();
saveGarage();
renderGarage();
return unlocked;
```
But `loadGarage` on init should also call unlockNewCars based on stored counts (in case schema). Then render.

`saveGarage` catches.

`renderGarage`:
```
garageGrid.innerHTML = PLAYER_CARS.map(spec => {
  const unlocked = isUnlocked(spec);
  const selected = garageSave.selected === spec.id;
  const stats = spec.stats.map((v,i)=>`<span class="car-stat"><span>${['SPD','ACC','GRP'][i]}</span><i><b style="width:${v*10}%;--car:${spec.color}"></b></i></span>`).join('');
  return `<button ... class="car-card ${...}" data-car="${spec.id}" ${unlocked?'':'disabled'} style="--car:${spec.color}">
   <span class="car-card-art">${carIcon(spec)}</span>
   <span class="car-card-name">${spec.name}</span>
   <span class="car-card-tag">${spec.tag}</span>
   <span class="car-stats">${stats}</span>
   ${unlocked ? `<span class="car-state">${selected?'SELECTED':'UNLOCKED'}</span>` : `<span class="car-state">LOCKED</span><span class="car-req">${spec.unlock.label}</span>`}
  </button>`;
}).join('');
garageProgress...
```
`--car` on button and bars uses var. Good. Inline `<b style="width:...">`, CSS background var(--car).

`openGarage`:
```
if (state.mode !== 'title') return;
garageScreen.classList.remove('hidden');
```
Maybe pause title attract? no.
`closeGarage`: add hidden.
`selectCar(id)`:
```
const spec = PLAYER_CARS.find...
if (!spec || !isUnlocked(spec)) return;
garageSave.selected = id;
saveGarage();
applyPlayerSetup();
renderGarage();
```
`applyPlayerSetup` also updates title dim.

Click listener:
```
garageGrid.addEventListener('click', e => {
 const btn = e.target.closest('[data-car]');
 if (btn) selectCar(btn.dataset.car);
});
```
Buttons disabled for locked; click won't fire.

`garageRaceBtn`: closeGarage(); startRace();

`garageCloseBtn`, `garageBackBtn`: closeGarage.
`garageScreen` click backdrop close: only if target === garageScreen.

Keydown Escape: existing listener toggles pause when Escape. If garage open and mode title, `pauseGame()` returns early, but we want close. Add at top of keydown:
```
if (event.code === 'Escape' && !garageScreen.classList.contains('hidden')) { closeGarage(); return; }
```
Also guard Enter when garage open: maybe close garage and start race? That's friendly:
```
if ((Enter) && state.mode === 'title') { if (garageOpen) closeGarage(); startRace(); }
```
But the existing handler is at bottom; leave. If garage open and user presses Enter, startRace hides title but garage remains open unless startRace hides garageScreen. Add in startRace: `garageScreen.classList.add('hidden');` So Enter starts race and hides garage. Good.

`startRace` hide garage. Good.

`showResults`: after rows and before resultsScreen remove hidden:
```
const unlocked = recordRaceResult(pos);
if (unlocked.length) { ... } else hidden
```
But recordRaceResult calls renderGarage which uses DOM; fine.

Also the results may show after player finishes; if the player finished 4th, still counts a race. Good.

Unlock note color: use inline style border-color? CSS gold. Fine:
```
unlockNote.innerHTML = `<b>New car${unlocked.length>1?'s':''} unlocked</b> — ${names}. Open the garage from the title screen.`;
unlockNote.classList.remove('hidden');
```
Maybe include names in `<b>` too. Keep simple.

Add `titleCarDot` style background update.

Potential issue: `applyPlayerSetup` called before `renderGarage` and before `playerCar` exists? We call in boot after everything. In `selectCar` playerCar exists. Fine.

Where to put functions relative to playerCar? After playerCar creation, but functions declared with `function` hoist. Constants `PLAYER_CARS` defined after playerCar. `loadGarage()` at boot after. Good.

Also need to apply initial setup before resetRace boot. Call at boot:
```
loadGarage();
unlockNewCars();
applyPlayerSetup();
renderGarage();
```
`unlockNewCars` may save. renderGarage displays.

One issue: `loadGarage` uses `garageSave` let? Use `const` object and mutate. Fine.

Now add DOM refs. Let me edit.

