In landscape, the car cards vanish (garage-list height 0). That's a real responsive bug (and a regression from the previous one-column grid). Need to fix the landscape layout: for short heights, use a horizontal layout where the 3D view is smaller and the list gets height, or stack the list under the view with a scrollable card.

Wait, why is .garage-list height 0 in the two-column grid? .garage-body height 138 (based on view?). The grid columns: view 552 wide? Actually view is 552 wide in a 554 body — meaning the grid is single-column (mobile media query applies since max-width: 820px? No, width 844 > 820 but pointer: coarse triggers the mobile query anyway). So the mobile query sets `.garage-body { grid-template-columns: 1fr; grid-template-rows: minmax(150px, 34vh) minmax(0, 1fr); }`. 34vh of 390 = 132.6 → minmax(150,132.6) = 150? view got 148 (border box?). The body has height 138 because the card fits content? Hmm, the card max-height 92vh = 359; card height 357. Head ~110 + body 138 + foot 60 + padding → 357. The body's rows: 148 + second row 0 (gap 10). Because `grid-template-rows: minmax(150px,34vh) minmax(0,1fr)` and the body has no explicit height → auto height = max(150, 34vh)=150 + second row auto (0 since content is scroll container with min-height 0). The list collapses because the body isn't stretched. The card is `display:flex; flex-direction:column;` and body `flex: 1 1 auto` with `min-height:0`. But the auto height from rows ends up 138... The card has max-height 359, but content doesn't stretch because the card also has no explicit height (max-height only), so flex items take content size. The view row is 150, list row 0.

Fix: In the short-landscape media query (max-height: 520px) and/or mobile query, ensure the garage body's second row has a minimum height and the card uses full height: e.g., `.garage-card { height: min(92vh, 780px) }` instead of max-height so flex distributes space. But on tall mobile, auto height is fine. Alternatively make `.garage-body { flex: 1 1 auto; min-height: 0; }` and set `.garage-card { height: min(92vh, 780px); }`. On desktop the card would be 780px tall even if content is smaller — the content would stretch (view/list grow). That's acceptable and often better. But the desktop garage screenshot currently has card height ~493px which looks balanced. Forcing 780px height would make it huge with a very tall preview. Not ideal.

Better: for the mobile/short screens, set explicit rows that account for viewport: e.g. in the `@media (pointer: coarse), (max-width: 820px)` block:
```
.garage-card { max-height: 92vh; height: min(92vh, 720px); }
```
Then body flex will distribute: head 110 + foot 60 + body 590 → rows: 34vh=132.6 (min 150) + second row gets remaining ~430. On mobile 844px tall: height = min(777, 720)=720; body ~545; view 287? Wait 34vh=287, second row 248 → good.

But the short-landscape query (max-height: 520px) needs a special layout because 390px height is tiny. In landscape short screens, maybe the garage should use a horizontal layout: view on the left with car, list on the right (two columns) to use horizontal space. The current mobile query forces one column. For short landscape, override back to two columns:
```
@media (max-height: 520px) and (orientation: landscape) {
  .garage-card { height: 94vh; max-height: 94vh; }
  .garage-body { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr); grid-template-rows: minmax(0,1fr); gap: 10px; margin: 8px 0; }
  .garage-view { min-height: 0; }
  .garage-list { min-height: 0; }
  .garage-head .garage-sub { display: none; }
  .garage-title { font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .garage-head .kicker { margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .garage-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 6px; }
}
```
The media query at line 1140 currently:
```
@media (max-height: 520px) and (orientation: landscape) {
  .title-screen { padding: 4vh 6vw; }
  .logo {...}
  ...
  .banner { top: 15%; }
}
```
