The `.garage-card` in the mobile query is `max-height: 92vh` (max 600px wide). On landscape 844px wide, the mobile media query applies because `(pointer: coarse)` (isMobile/touch) even though width > 820. The `.panel-card` width min(480) → card width min(600,100%) → measured 598. Two problems: the mobile layout is single column and the list collapses.

Best fix for short landscape: in the `@media (max-height: 520px) and (orientation: landscape)` query, add garage overrides:

```
  .garage-card { width: min(780px, 100%); max-height: 94vh; height: 94vh; }
  .garage-body {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.85fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr);
    grid-template-rows: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 10px;
    margin: 8px 0;
  }
  .garage-view { min-height: 0; }
  .garage-list { min-height: 0; overflow-y: auto; }
  .garage-head .kicker { margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .garage-title { font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 2px; }
  .garage-sub { display: none; }
  .garage-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 6px; }
  .car-card-art { width: 26px; height: 40px; }
  .garage-foot { padding-top: 8px; }
```

With height 94vh = 367; head ~64 (kicker + title, sub hidden), foot ~60, body → 367 - padding 48 - head 64 - foot 60 - margins 16 = ~179 for body. List 179 tall, scrollable with 2 rows of cards (each ~145px?) → scroll. 3 columns × 2 rows; each card in compact styles (mobile card padding 12px 8px, art 52px, name, tag, stats 3 bars, state). Card height ~150. So 2 rows = 307 > 179 → scrollable. That's acceptable; user can scroll. Alternatively 5 columns × 1 row to fit all: grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr) with compact cards ~100px wide each; list width ~330; each card 62px wide — too narrow for stats but maybe okay. Better 3 columns and allow scroll, or 3 columns × 2 rows and reduce card content. Scroll is fine.

Let's also reduce the garage head: the title 24px, hide sub. That gives more room.

But wait: with `.garage-card { height: 94vh; }` and the base `display:flex; flex-direction: column; overflow:hidden`, the body flex item will fill. Body has `flex: 1 1 auto; min-height: 0` from base. Good. The grid rows `minmax(0,1fr)` for the single row.

Also ensure the list scroll works within grid: `.garage-list` already `min-height:0; overflow-y:auto` in base. Good.

Let me also consider portrait small phones 360x640: mobile query gives single column, view 34vh=218 (min150), body flex:1. Card max-height 92vh=589 but no height → content height may exceed and overflow hidden (the card has overflow hidden). Let me verify on 390x844 it's fine (it was). On 640 height: head ~120 + body rows: view max(150, 217)=217 + second row auto: content 2 rows × ~150 = 300 → body 527, foot 60 + paddings 50 + head 120 = 757 > 589 max-height... The card would overflow hidden and the foot might be cut off! The body's second row is `minmax(0,1fr)` within an auto-height grid: auto height means rows size to content? `minmax(0,1fr)` with indefinite container height behaves as max-content. So body = 217 + 300 = 517 + gaps; card content ~757; with max-height 589 and `overflow:hidden`, foot clipped? In the mobile 390x844 test, card fits (92vh=776, content maybe 640). On a 640px-tall phone, content 757 > 589 → clipping. The previous 2D garage used max-height 90vh with the grid maybe also overflowed. Hmm.

A robust approach: make the garage card always `height: min(92vh, 780px)` for the mobile/short screens, so the body flex-shrinks and the list scrolls. Add in the mobile query:
```
.garage-card { height: min(92vh, 720px); }
```
Wait, if head+foot+padding are large, body gets the rest and the list scrolls within. This guarantees no clipping. On a portrait phone: 92vh = 589 (640). Head ~110, foot 60, paddings 48 → body ~370; rows: view minmax(150, 34vh=218) + list 142 (scroll). 3-col grid cards 150 tall → scroll needed. Acceptable. On 390x844: height=min(776,720)=720 → body ~500; view 287 + list 203 → scroll for 2 rows (300). Hmm, previously on 390x844 the list was NOT scrollable (all 5 cards visible, 2 rows). Now it would need scrolling because view takes 34vh=287 and list only ~200. That's a slight downgrade. 

Alternative: only add height for short viewports (max-height: 700px). Use a separate media query for `(pointer: coarse), (max-width: 820px)` with no height change, and add `@media (max-height: 700px) { .garage-card { height: min(92vh, 700px); } }` maybe combined with orientation. Hmm, complexity.

Simplest robust: In the mobile query, keep `max-height: 92vh` but add `.garage-body { min-height: 0; }` and let the grid be `grid-template-rows: minmax(120px, 30vh) minmax(0, 1fr); flex: 1 1 auto;`. The real issue in landscape was the row heights not having a container height. The card's content height exceeded max-height? No: in landscape, card height 357 (max 359). The body wasn't given the remaining space because the flex container's height is max-content, and max-height clamps the box but doesn't stretch children. When content is taller than max-height, it overflows and gets clipped (not shrunk) unless children have flex-shrink. `.garage-body` has `flex: 1 1 auto` and `min-height: 0`, so it should shrink when the container is constrained by max-height... In flexbox, max-height on the flex container does constrain flex items? Apparently it does shrink, but the grid rows then use percentages/auto. The body shrank to 138 and its rows: 150 (min) + 0. So in landscape, the view took 148 and the list 0. The list could have taken minmax(0,1fr) → 0 because there was no space. So the view's min 150 + gap consumed the body. Total card content: head 110 + body 138 + foot 60 = 308 + padding ~48 = 356. That fits 357! The list got 0 because the body was only 138, with 148 for the view and 10 gap. The card's max-height 359 was hit before the list could get space — because the view row got 34vh=132.6 clamped to min 150, and the head/foot are large at mobile sizes. So the fix is to shrink the view row on short screens (e.g., 90px) and let the list take the rest.

So add short-landscape overrides: two columns with view height = full body height (~180) and list to the right; both get decent space. With two columns, the car view gets ~250x180, list ~300x180 scrollable. That's better than single column with a 148px view and zero list.

Let me implement the landscape override as two columns and slightly smaller header. Set `.garage-card { width: min(820px, 100%); height: 92vh; }` to ensure distribution. Let me make sure the body gets `min-height: 0` and rows `minmax(0, 1fr)`; with explicit card height, flex distributes.

Also test 360x640 portrait to ensure no clipping. Use height: auto? I'll test after.

